{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"DOI:\"10.7326/m18-2101\"","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":1,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"30831578","source":"MED","pmid":"30831578","doi":"10.7326/m18-2101","title":"Measles, Mumps, Rubella Vaccination and Autism: A Nationwide Cohort Study.","authorString":"Hviid A, Hansen JV, Frisch M, Melbye M.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Hviid A","firstName":"Anders","lastName":"Hviid","initials":"A","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7509-9127"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Statens Serum Institut, Copenhagen, Denmark (A.H., J.V.H., M.F.)."}]}},{"fullName":"Hansen JV","firstName":"Jørgen Vinsløv","lastName":"Hansen","initials":"JV","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0494-4100"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Statens Serum Institut, Copenhagen, Denmark (A.H., J.V.H., M.F.)."}]}},{"fullName":"Frisch M","firstName":"Morten","lastName":"Frisch","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3864-8860"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Statens Serum Institut, Copenhagen, Denmark (A.H., J.V.H., M.F.)."}]}},{"fullName":"Melbye M","firstName":"Mads","lastName":"Melbye","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8264-6785"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Statens Serum Institut and University of Copenhagen, Copenhagen, Denmark, Stanford University School of Medicine, Stanford, California (M.M.)."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8264-6785"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0494-4100"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3864-8860"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7509-9127"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["recommended_reviews"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"8","volume":"170","journalIssueId":2806483,"dateOfPublication":"2019 Apr","monthOfPublication":4,"yearOfPublication":2019,"printPublicationDate":"2019-04-01","journal":{"title":"Annals of internal medicine","medlineAbbreviation":"Ann Intern Med","essn":"1539-3704","issn":"0003-4819","isoabbreviation":"Ann Intern Med","nlmid":"0372351"}},"pubYear":"2019","pageInfo":"513-520","abstractText":"<h4>Background</h4>The hypothesized link between the measles, mumps, rubella (MMR) vaccine and autism continues to cause concern and challenge vaccine uptake.<h4>Objective</h4>To evaluate whether the MMR vaccine increases the risk for autism in children, subgroups of children, or time periods after vaccination.<h4>Design</h4>Nationwide cohort study.<h4>Setting</h4>Denmark.<h4>Participants</h4>657 461 children born in Denmark from 1999 through 31 December 2010, with follow-up from 1 year of age and through 31 August 2013.<h4>Measurements</h4>Danish population registries were used to link information on MMR vaccination, autism diagnoses, other childhood vaccines, sibling history of autism, and autism risk factors to children in the cohort. Survival analysis of the time to autism diagnosis with Cox proportional hazards regression was used to estimate hazard ratios of autism according to MMR vaccination status, with adjustment for age, birth year, sex, other childhood vaccines, sibling history of autism, and autism risk factors (based on a disease risk score).<h4>Results</h4>During 5 025 754 person-years of follow-up, 6517 children were diagnosed with autism (incidence rate, 129.7 per 100 000 person-years). Comparing MMR-vaccinated with MMR-unvaccinated children yielded a fully adjusted autism hazard ratio of 0.93 (95% CI, 0.85 to 1.02). Similarly, no increased risk for autism after MMR vaccination was consistently observed in subgroups of children defined according to sibling history of autism, autism risk factors (based on a disease risk score) or other childhood vaccinations, or during specified time periods after vaccination.<h4>Limitation</h4>No individual medical charts were reviewed.<h4>Conclusion</h4>The study strongly supports that MMR vaccination does not increase the risk for autism, does not trigger autism in susceptible children, and is not associated with clustering of autism cases after vaccination. It adds to previous studies through significant additional statistical power and by addressing hypotheses of susceptible subgroups and clustering of cases.<h4>Primary funding source</h4>Novo Nordisk Foundation and Danish Ministry of Health.","affiliation":"Statens Serum Institut, Copenhagen, Denmark (A.H., J.V.H., M.F.).","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"grantId":"NNF14OC0008847","agency":"Novo Nordisk Fonden","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Novo Nordisk Fonden","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Disease Susceptibility"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Measles-Mumps-Rubella Vaccine","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"AE","qualifierName":"adverse effects","majorTopic_YN":"Y"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Vaccination","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"AE","qualifierName":"adverse effects","majorTopic_YN":"Y"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Registries"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Proportional Hazards Models"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Risk Factors"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cohort Studies"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Siblings"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Autistic Disorder","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ET","qualifierName":"etiology","majorTopic_YN":"Y"},{"abbreviation":"EP","qualifierName":"epidemiology","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Adolescent"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Child"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Child, Preschool"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Infant"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Denmark","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"EP","qualifierName":"epidemiology","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Female"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Male"}]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"Measles-Mumps-Rubella Vaccine","registryNumber":"0"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.7326/M18-2101"}]},"commentCorrectionList":{"commentCorrection":[{"id":"30831577","source":"MED","reference":"Ann Intern Med. 2019 Apr 16;170(8):567-568. doi: 10.7326/M19-0596","type":"Comment in","orderIn":1},{"id":"31217233","source":"MED","reference":"BMJ Evid Based Med. 2019 Oct;24(5):198-199. doi: 10.1136/bmjebm-2019-111212","type":"Comment in","orderIn":2},{"id":"31476223","source":"MED","reference":"Ann Intern Med. 2019 Sep 3;171(5):387-388. doi: 10.7326/L19-0381","type":"Comment in","orderIn":3},{"id":"31476224","source":"MED","reference":"Ann Intern Med. 2019 Sep 3;171(5):386-387. doi: 10.7326/L19-0382","type":"Comment in","orderIn":4},{"id":"31476225","source":"MED","reference":"Ann Intern Med. 2019 Sep 3;171(5):388. doi: 10.7326/L19-0383","type":"Comment in","orderIn":5}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","citedByCount":108,"hasData":"N","hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasLabsLinks":"Y","hasEvaluations":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCompletion":"2020-01-21","dateOfCreation":"2019-03-05","firstIndexDate":"2019-03-05","dateOfRevision":"2022-04-09","electronicPublicationDate":"2019-03-05","firstPublicationDate":"2019-03-05"}]}}